{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/36928-thought-experiment-the-faceless-angels-are-angels","id":36928,"title":"Thought Experiment- the Faceless Angels ARE Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-25T08:30:07-08:00","id":36928,"title":"Thought Experiment- the Faceless Angels ARE Angels","content":"yes, the Faceless Angels of the Knights of St. George are abyssal entities in all but the name, and there is a pretty good chance they are not less but the Annunaki- the very beings which dreams the Abyss. But let us assume, just for a second, that we know nothing about the Abyss, Mage and cosmology, and try to turn the Faceless Angels from the creators of the Abyss into something else- the angels of the God Machine (not much of an improvement, but hey, you could always choose Inferno next time :P)<br /> <br /> So, how does it works?<br /> <br /> Like many 6+ entities (spirits, archmasters, archdemons, etc), we can assume that archangels are creatures which are so &quot;great&quot; that they are formed into number of bodies. In that case, all of the 72 Faceless Angels could be, actually, a single being with a single mission- to keep take magic from the world and feed it to the God Machine. Why? It could be an experiment of the God Machine in which it tries to convert Mana/ Source into Essence. It could be that the God Machine needs that energy in order to work, or perhaps it use it to feed its angels. I think that the simplest option is that it convert it to Essence- like, Mana gets into the Faceless Angels, transformed, and when it gets out it can feed the God Machine. We can assume that, in that case, the God Machine probably have similar mechanism for other energies (Vitae, Plasm, etc) but this is not important.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the problem is that the God Machine gave the Angels one mission- collect Source/ Mana/ whatever. And the Archangel, like any faithful one, has obeyed- the problem was that it couldn't do it efficiently enough. After all, the Supernal Realms are without of its grasp. In order to fulfill its mission, it started to search after other sources of energy, like Hallows, Nods or mages. Being an Archangel, it didn't really cared about how much destruction it caused as long as it fulfilled its mission- and as an archangel, we can assume it made enough destruction in its search after ley lines and Supernal energy. That was the time when the forefathers of the Knights understood that they had to stop it- one way or another.<br /> <br /> So they sacrificed him a witch. Sure, it must have been painful, for the chances are that the witch has served her community faithfully, but it was for the greater good. And while they sacrificed the witch, they have also offerd it a deal- to let them search for the energy it sought for in a much less destructive way. The archangel, like any loyal angel of the Machine, has computed the loss vs gain and concluded that letting other people work for it wasted less resources than actually seeking after them by itself. And so, it agreed to go to sleep- but warned them that if it won't gain enough energy it will awaken. In a way, it may be the angel Marco Singe talked about when he spoke about the angel who would stay asleep as long as the tribe would sing for it, with the &quot;songs&quot; being Mana.<br /> <br /> So what about the Geotic Gospels? Well, that's simple enough. When the archangel went to sleep, it created a connection between the Knights and itself, so they could feed it with magic. However, the connection works for both ways, and allows the Knights to connect with the dreams of the archangels. The so called &quot;geotic demons&quot; are actually neither geotic not demons. they are the memetic dreams of the angel, and because hubris is so common in mages that it became part of their souls, and the archangel eat those souls, he dreams about the sins of mankind- and those dreams, those memes, are used by the Knights. That means that the faceless Angels are truly the ones behind the Tunguska event, when the Knights didn't fed it with enough magic so it started to search alone. That means that the Knights aren't dupes and fools that serve something without understanding they do more harm than help. It means that the Knights actually do the right thing, and those sins upon themselves. They actually do protect the world...<br /> <br /> Or not. Didn't you heard? The Knights lie all the time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T12:59:57-08:00","id":36992,"title":"","content":"It actually works quite nicely, I'm quite impressed. However, they're still dupes and fools. They're still a cult who recruit through Anglicanism while having completely alternate belief system. Further, the deal itself is little better, you're still serving the aims of an alien entity whose motives you don't know.<br /> <br /> That's all assuming that the original Knights weren't in fact right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T15:56:46-08:00","id":37049,"title":"","content":"Where do you get the idea that they're Abyssal entities in the first place? In the writeup that's just a suggestion, right after them being Supernal beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T16:29:36-08:00","id":37061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/36928-thought-experiment-the-faceless-angels-are-angels?p=36992#post36992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It actually works quite nicely, I'm quite impressed. However, they're still dupes and fools. They're still a cult who recruit through Anglicanism while having completely alternate belief system. Further, the deal itself is little better, you're still serving the aims of an alien entity whose motives you don't know.<br /> <br /> That's all assuming that the original Knights weren't in fact right.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I wrote that the &quot;Knights aren't dupes and fools that serve something without understanding they do more harm than help&quot;, I didn't meant they aren't fools and dupes anymore- but that they are dupes which do the right thing in saving the world. Their faith is true, and they actually do protect the world and not feed the Abyss. And about that they lie to their own members- well, this is their theme, isn't it? Also, like I've said in the beginning, it is not much of an improvement- and after making them astral beings and angels of the God Machine, maybe making them into demons of Inferno is the next take :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T16:39:31-08:00","id":37063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/36928-thought-experiment-the-faceless-angels-are-angels?p=37049#post37049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you get the idea that they're Abyssal entities in the first place? In the writeup that's just a suggestion, right after them being Supernal beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is kind of a consensus in almost anyone I've met here in the forums. I mean, a Lovecraftian being + cult structure + hate toward magic (especially the dragons) + the way some of their fluff was presented (like the Lucifuge stereotype) = (usually) an Abyssal being. The presentation of the Annunaki from Left Handed Path pretty resembled the Faceless Angels in so many ways, that making them nothing other than an abyssal being sounded ridiculous. What I'm trying to do is to show (mostly to myself) that there are still other ways to look at them that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T02:18:47-08:00","id":37247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but that they are dupes which do the right thing in saving the world. Their faith is true, and they actually do protect the world and not feed the Abyss. </div> </div> </div>Who says they didn't protect the world in the original version? And who says they're saving the world now? They're still handing people to a faceless entity with horrible designs for the world in return for it not destroying the world today. That's the exact same deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}